## Bug Decription
The free5gc SMF can be crashed remotely by a malformed PFCP SessionReportRequest sent by a UPF (or an attacker spoofing a UPF). When the report sets ReportType.USAR=1 and includes a UsageReport IE, but omits the UsageReportTrigger sub-IE, SMF dereferences a nil pointer while determining the trigger type and panics, terminating the SMF process (DoS).

Based on the stack trace, the crash occurs in internal/context/identityTriggerType() at pfcp_reports.go:77, which is called from SMContext.HandleReports() (pfcp_reports.go:29) via HandlePfcpSessionReportRequest() (internal/pfcp/handler/handler.go:195). The code path accesses usarTrigger.Volth even when the UsageReportTrigger IE is missing, causing a nil pointer dereference.

