./cmake-build-release/nr-cli <gnb-node> -e "ue-list"
./cmake-build-release/nr-cli <gnb-node> -e "ue-release <ue-id>"
```

stop the UE process after `ue-release` to avoid immediate
reattach, so the session stays deactivated.

4) The fake UPF waits for a `SessionModificationRequest` that indicates
buffering (`UpdateFAR` with `ApplyAction.BUFF=1`). After that signal is
seen, it sends the malformed `SessionReportRequest` (no
`DownlinkDataReport`) to SMF.

## Expected Behavior
SMF should validate PFCP message consistency:
If ReportType.DLDR is set but DownlinkDataReport is missing, SMF should reject/ignore the report and/or respond with an appropriate PFCP error cause without crashing.
SMF must not panic due to malformed PFCP input.
Ideally, PFCP message dispatch should include panic recovery so one malformed message cannot terminate the process.

