./cmake-build-release/nr-cli <gnb-node> -e "ue-release <ue-id>"
```

stop the UE process after `ue-release` to avoid immediate
reattach, so the session stays deactivated.

4) The fake UPF waits for a SessionModificationRequest that indicates
buffering (UpdateFAR with ApplyAction.BUFF=1). After that signal is
seen, it sends the malformed SessionReportRequest with ReportType.USAR=1 and a UsageReport IE present, but deliberately omits the VolumeMeasurement sub-IE inside the UsageReport, triggering a nil pointer dereference in SMF.

## Expected Behavior
SMF should validate that UsageReport contains required sub-IEs when ReportType.USAR is set.

If VolumeMeasurement is missing, SMF should reject the SessionReportRequest gracefully (e.g., respond with an error/cause) and continue running.

PFCP handler goroutines should not be able to crash the whole SMF process (panic recovery / defensive checks).

